message.content:
Sentence 7 and 8 give a reason: the general obligation to manage risks to data subjects' rights and freedoms persists even when DPIA triggers aren't met. That is a substantive purpose (risk management), not "law requires it." Sentence 8 is the same in substance.

Sentence 11 says the controller must assess whether high risk is likely as part of accountability, but it gives no purpose beyond accountability, so it is partial at most. Sentences 5 and 6 state an obligation only. Sentences 1 and 2 restate the seed (accountability obligations), which is essentially "law requires it." Sentences 3, 4, 9, 10 are exemptions. Sentence 12 is a definition.

{"states": [7, 8], "partially": [11], "reason": "Sentences 7 and 8 tie the assessment to managing risks to data subjects' rights and freedoms; 11 only gestures at accountability and assessing high risk."}
